  the second positional is the message that kicks off the new branch.
  \`--from <id|self>\` is an alias for the positional source.

  \`sessions branch\` forks an existing conversation into a brand-new session
  whose transcript is a copy of the source's transcript up to (and including)
  the user's first new message (issue #364). The first turn of the new branch
  can run on a different \`--provider\` / \`--model\` / \`--mode\` than the
  source; later turns use whatever the user picks in the composer (the
  source's defaults). With no override flags the first turn runs on the same
  agent/model/mode as the source — useful for "continue this conversation in
  a sibling session". The branch marker (\`[/branch: codex->claude/opus-5] …\`)
  is recorded as the first message so the chat view audits which agent/model
  ran the first turn. \`--title\` overrides the auto-generated
  \`Branch of <sourceTitle>\`. The new session is recorded as a child of the
  source (\`controller sessions list --parent <sourceId>\` and
  \`controller sessions children <sourceId>\` both surface it) so the sidebar
  subtree groups every branch under its source.

